Subject: [PATCH] S4: Full Swagger documentation for Transfers & Disposal
 modules
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Covers TransactionsController, CardDisposalsController (8 endpoints
— the most complex business rules in the API; TransferErrors.cs
alone has 30+ codes).

- Add Swagger/Examples/TransactionsExamples.cs, CardDisposalExamples.cs
  and register them in ExampleCatalog.
- Backfill missing <response> XML doc tags on all 8 actions.
- Fix a real pre-existing doc-comment bug: CardDisposalsController's
  class doc claimed no read-only admin path exists at all on this
  controller. Confirmed by reading DisposalService.ResolveReadScope
  directly that GetAll/GetById DO give a system admin cross-tenant
  read access, exactly like TransactionsController's reads -- only
  the write path (Dispose) rejects an admin token. Corrected.
- Confirm Transfer.ActorNotResolved is, per its own doc comment,
  unreachable behind [Authorize] with a valid tenant token --
  documented as such rather than given a misleading 'reachable'
  example, unlike the genuinely-reachable ActorNotResolved variants
  on other controllers (S1-S3).
- Continue the SystemAdminNotAllowed (Forbidden, enveloped) pattern
  from S2 on Transfer.SystemAdminNotAllowed / Disposal.SystemAdminNotAllowed.
- Given TransferErrors.cs's size, examples cover only the most
  illustrative scenario per response code, not an exhaustive
  enumeration -- the source file remains authoritative for the full
  catalogue.
- Update Docs/PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE.md (§3, §18, metadata trailer) with
  S4 coverage and both new findings.

Only BranchRequestsController remains, planned for S5.
